(
K04 incnav3 (2026-10-06): group_materi_expansion_volume reduces the
density rho = rho0*(1 - beta*T) in the momentum inertia as well as in the
gravity force (Pro test incnav3: T = 0.5, beta = 1 -> rho = 0.5; the
expansion and gravity forces give a velocity rate of -2.5/rho = -5).
One step of 0.01: tvely(2) = -4.990415335 = Professional 02-08-2026
(-4.990415335463). GNU before K04: -2.4976 (inertia with rho0).
The legacy sfnet incnav3 (target -2.5) predates this Professional
convention (BACKLOG B11).
)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
derivatives
condif_temperature
materi_velocity
materi_stress
end_initia

mesh -fixed_in_space -fixed_in_space
inertia_apply -yes

node 1  0  0
node 2  1  0
node 3  1  1
node 4  0  1
element 1  -quad4  1 2 4 3

bounda_dof 0  -ra 1 2 3 4 -ra -temp
bounda_time    0  0.0 0.5 100. 0.5

force_gravity 0. 1.

group_type 0  -materi
group_materi_density 0  1.0
group_materi_expansion_linear 0  1.
group_materi_expansion_volume 0  1.
group_materi_elasti_compressibility 0  1.0
group_materi_memory 0  -updated_linear

print_filter 0  -node_dof -all -tvely

control_timestep 0  0.01 0.01

target_item 0  -node_dof 2 -tvely
target_value   0  -4.990415335 1.e-6
end_data
